        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62280,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62281,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>It occurs mostly in the second and third decades of life, presenting with abdominal pain and/or pelvic mass {25395492}. Most patients have a high level of serum AFP. YST may coexist with ovarian or endometrial cancer in older patients {21804392; 27334714; 29106744; 8764742}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-29T16:18:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62282,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It accounts for 20% of malignant ovarian germ cell tumours {16648414}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62283,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62284,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>About 75% of cases have chromosome&nbsp;12 abnormality, mostly isochromosome 12p {9679978}. In older women with coexisting ovarian or endometrial carcinoma, the YST is thought to be of somatic tumour origin {21804392; 27334714; 29106744}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-29T16:19:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62285,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is unilateral, large (average: 15&nbsp;cm), solid, and cystic, with a friable, haemorrhagic, necrotic appearance {63318}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62286,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Multiple patterns are usually present, most commonly a reticular/microcystic pattern (a meshwork of anastomosing spaces and cysts lined by a single layer of tumour cells) {63318; 22008025; 25395492}. Other patterns include the endodermal sinus pattern (a proliferation of Schiller&ndash;Duval bodies, which are round or elongated tumour cell&ndash;lined papillae with a large central vessel, protruding into a cystic space surrounded by tumour cells) {22008025}, papillary pattern, solid pattern, festoon pattern (complex ribbons and undulating cords), and glandular pattern (endometrioid-like or intestinal-type) {3661822; 22008025; 27443515}. Less common patterns are the polyvesicular-vitelline pattern (numerous vesicles and cysts within cellular stroma) {63318; 23348213}, parietal pattern (tumour cells embedded in linear bands of basement membrane material), mesenchyme-like pattern (tumour cells scattered in oedematous or myxomatous connective tissue), and hepatoid pattern {7139531}. Tumour cell appearance depends on the growth pattern, but the cells usually exhibit variable atypia, clear cytoplasm, and hyaline globules. In older women with a coexisting ovarian or endometrial carcinoma, YST typically exhibits a reticular pattern {28581124; 8764742}.</p>\r\n<p>Positive immunohistochemical markers (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/2/13160\" target=\"_blank\">#13160</a>Table <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/2/13160\" target=\"_blank\">#13160</a>) include SALL4 {19295406}, LIN28 {22034885}, AFP (often focal and weak), glypican-3 (GPC3) {18277882}, and ZBTB16 {26916077}, as well as CDX2 in the intestinal-type pattern, Hep&nbsp;Par-1 in the hepatoid pattern, and TTF1 in the foregut/respiratory pattern {24444105; 27443515}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-09T15:19:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62287,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 87,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:52:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
